 "system": "n64",
 "_ergonomics": "The stick sits where a d-pad sits everywhere else, since it is this pad's primary input, not a secondary one. C-buttons cluster on the right the way they do on the real pad, banded so a diagonal (C-up-right for the camera) falls out of the overlap the same way the main d-pad's diagonals do elsewhere. Z is a face button, not a shoulder, deliberately: on the real hardware it's a trigger under the pad, but that position is a bad reach on a flat touchscreen, so it sits with A and B instead, for thumb convenience over hardware accuracy. Input ids were rewritten 2026-08-11 for the native graduation: mupen64plus-libretro-nx's own controller mapping (spikes/cores/mupen64plus/src/custom/mupen64plus-core/plugin/emulate_game_controller_via_libretro.c) puts N64 A/B on RetroPad B/Y (0/1), N64 L shoulder on RetroPad Select (2), N64 R shoulder on RetroPad R2 (13), Z on RetroPad L2 (12), and the four C-buttons on RetroPad X/A/L/R (9/8/10/11, up/down/left/right) rather than a second analog stick. The ids this file carried from an earlier, reverted native attempt did not match that table and have been corrected against it directly, not reused.",
